    {
      "title": "Jaishankar slams global energy disruptions through sanctions, chokepoints",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/external-affairs-defence-security/news/jaishankar-slams-global-energy-disruptions-through-sanctions-chokepoints-126103100067_1.html",
      "description": "External Affairs Minister S Jaishankar strongly disapproved of disruptions in global oil supplies through sanctions and chokepoints, saying deliberate attacks on energy trade and infrastructure were a calculated strategy to hold prices hostage.\nJaishankar's remarks at the G20 Foreign Ministers' Meeting in Atlanta on Friday came amid American sanctions on the sale of Iranian oil and disruption to energy supplies from West Asia and the decision to lift sanctions on the sale of Russian diesel.\nThe minister said that the world was staring at an energy crisis not of production, but of unpredictability and disruption, unaffordable costs, and challenges of access.\nJaishankar, in a post on X, said he highlighted that deliberate attacks on energy trade and infrastructure were a calculated strategy to hold energy prices hostage.\n\"The G20 must display both understanding and leadership to keep energy markets open and predictable,\" he said at the meeting convened by US Secretary of State Marco",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-31T02:40:00"
    }
